# MCP Management UI

Patterns for building MCP plugin management interfaces. These were established during the MCP Management settings page implementation (feat/mcp-library-and-management, v4.0.3-canary.5+).

## Settings page integration

To add a new settings tab:

| Layer | File |
|---|---|
| Enum | `src/store/global/initialState.ts` — add to `SettingsTabs` enum |
| Sidebar | `src/app/[variants]/(main)/settings/hooks/useCategory.tsx` — add menu item |
| Component map | `src/app/[variants]/(main)/settings/_layout/SettingsContent.tsx` — add `dynamic(() => import('...'))` entry |
| Page | `src/app/[variants]/(main)/settings/<tab>/index.tsx` — the page component |
| i18n | `src/locales/default/setting.ts` + `locales/en-US|zh-CN/setting.json` — `tab.<key>` + page-specific keys |

## Two-panel layout (list + detail)

MCP management pages should use a two-panel pattern matching `PluginStore/InstalledList`:

```tsx
// Top bar: search + action buttons
<Flexbox align={'center'} gap={8} horizontal justify={'space-between'}>
  <Input placeholder="Search..." prefix={<Search />} />
  <Flexbox gap={8} horizontal>
    <Button icon={PackagePlus} onClick={handleAdd}>Add MCP Plugin</Button>
    <Button icon={Store} onClick={openStore}>Plugin Store</Button>
  </Flexbox>
</Flexbox>

// Two-column body
<Flexbox flex={1} horizontal style={{ borderTop, overflow: 'hidden' }}>
  {/* Left: scrollable list with DraggablePanel */}
  <DraggablePanel maxWidth={540} minWidth={320} placement={'left'}>
    <Flexbox height={'100%'} style={{ overflowY: 'auto' }}>
      {filteredList.map(item => (
        <PluginItem
          active={selectedId === item.identifier}
          onClick={() => select(item)}
          runtimeType={plugin.runtimeType}
          type="plugin"
          {...item}
        />
      ))}
    </Flexbox>
  </DraggablePanel>

  {/* Right: detail panel */}
  {selectedId ? (
    <Flexbox style={{ background: token.colorBgContainerSecondary }} width={'100%'}>
      <DetailPanel id={selectedId} onEdit={openEdit} onUninstall={handleUninstall} />
    </Flexbox>
  ) : (
    <Empty description="Select a plugin" />
  )}
</Flexbox>
```

Reference: `src/features/PluginStore/InstalledList/index.tsx` + `List/index.tsx` + `List/Item/index.tsx`

## PluginDevModal: edit mode CRITICAL — key prop for remount

`PluginDevModal` (`src/features/PluginDevModal/index.tsx`) populates its Ant Design `Form` in a `useEffect` that runs **only on mount**:

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  form.setFieldsValue(value);
}, []); // empty deps — runs once
```

**Without a `key` prop, switching between plugins leaves stale form data.**

The existing `EditCustomPlugin` wrapper (`src/features/PluginStore/InstalledList/EditCustomPlugin.tsx`) solves this:

```tsx
<DevModal
  key={identifier}     // ← FORCES remount when identifier changes
  mode={'edit'}
  onOpenChange={onOpenChange}
  onSave={async (devPlugin) => { await installCustomPlugin(devPlugin); }}
  onValueChange={updateNewDevPlugin}
  open={open}
  value={customPlugin} // LobeToolCustomPlugin from store
/>
```

**ALWAYS pass `key={identifier || 'create'}` to `PluginDevModal`** when the modal can switch between different plugins or between create/edit modes. This forces React to unmount and remount the component, which triggers `form.setFieldsValue(value)` with the correct data.

### PluginDevModal props

| Prop | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `mode` | `'create'` or `'edit'` | Controls drawer title and footer |
| `open` | `boolean` | |
| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` | |
| `value` | `LobeToolCustomPlugin` | The plugin data to pre-fill (edit mode) |
| `onSave` | `(value: LobeToolCustomPlugin) => Promise<void>` | Call `installCustomPlugin` (create) or `updateCustomPlugin` (edit) |
| `onDelete` | `() => void` | Edit mode only — call `uninstallCustomPlugin` |
| `onValueChange` | `(value: Partial<LobeToolCustomPlugin>) => void` | Always pass `updateNewCustomPlugin` from store |
| `key` | `string` | **CRITICAL** — `identifier` for edit, `'create'` for add |

## Filtering installed plugins to MCP-only

Installed plugins live in `useToolStore(pluginSelectors.installedPlugins)`. MCP plugins are those with `customParams?.mcp`:

```typescript
const installedPlugins = useToolStore(pluginSelectors.installedPlugins, isEqual);
const mcpPlugins = installedPlugins.filter(p => !!p.customParams?.mcp);
```

For the list display (with metadata like title, description, avatar), use `pluginSelectors.installedPluginMetaList`:

```typescript
const installedMetaList = useToolStore(pluginSelectors.installedPluginMetaList, isEqual);
```

## Install / update / uninstall via store

```typescript
const [installCustomPlugin, updateCustomPlugin, uninstallCustomPlugin, updateNewDevPlugin] =
  useToolStore((s) => [
    s.installCustomPlugin,   // create new plugin
    s.updateCustomPlugin,    // update existing (id, value)
    s.uninstallCustomPlugin, // remove by identifier
    s.updateNewCustomPlugin, // update draft state for DevModal
  ]);
```

Always call `useFetchInstalledPlugins()` to load the installed plugin list from the database on mount.

## Empty state

When no MCP plugins are installed, show an `Empty` component with buttons to add a plugin or open the store:

```tsx
<Center height={'75vh'} paddingBlock={40}>
  <Empty description={t('mcpManagement.empty')} image={Empty.PRESENTED_IMAGE_SIMPLE}>
    <Flexbox gap={8} horizontal justify={'center'}>
      <Button icon={PackagePlus} onClick={handleAdd}>Add MCP Plugin</Button>
      <Button icon={Store} onClick={() => setShowStore(true)}>Plugin Store</Button>
    </Flexbox>
  </Empty>
</Center>
```

## i18n key discipline

**Always verify i18n keys against the locale source files before using them.** Do not invent key names from patterns or assumptions — check the actual definitions.

Example bug (v4.0.3-canary.8 fix): used `tPlugin('store.searchPlaceholder')` on the search input, but the `plugin` namespace only defines `store.placeholder`:

```ts
// Correct key in src/locales/default/plugin.ts:
store: {
  placeholder: '搜索插件名称介绍或关键词...', // ← this is the actual key
  // ... no searchPlaceholder exists
}
```

When adding a search input to an MCP/plugin management page:
- `tPlugin('store.placeholder')` — the search placeholder for plugin/list views
- `tPlugin('store.emptySelectHint')` — shown when no list item is selected in detail panel
- `tPlugin('store.empty')` — shown when no plugins are installed

All three keys are in the `plugin` namespace (`useTranslation('plugin')`), not in `setting` or `discover`.

## Store browser modal

`PluginStore` (`src/features/PluginStore/index.tsx`) opens as a modal with `open` / `setOpen` props. It renders `PluginStore/Content` which has tabs for browsing installed plugins and the marketplace.
